.TH "REPROCTL\-RESTART" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-restart \- rebuild services or restart Tilt
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl restart\f[R] \f[I]service\f[R] [\f[I]service\f[R]\&...]
| \f[B]\(enall\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rebuild and redeploy running services, or restart the entire Tilt
daemon.
.PP
Without \f[B]\(enall\f[R], triggers a rebuild of the specified services
via \f[B]tilt trigger\f[R].
If a service has an associated migration resource, the migration is
triggered first.
.PP
With \f[B]\(enall\f[R], the Tilt daemon is stopped and restarted while
preserving the current service configuration from
\f[B]reproctl_services.json\f[R].
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enall\f[R]
Stop and restart the Tilt daemon instead of rebuilding individual
services.
.TP
\f[B]\(enpick\f[R], \f[B]\-p\f[R]
Interactively select a service to restart.
Uses \f[B]fzf\f[R] if installed, otherwise a numbered prompt.
When no service names are given and stdin is a terminal, the picker is
shown automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl restart api\-server
Rebuild and redeploy api\-server.
.TP
reproctl restart api\-server workspace
Rebuild multiple services.
.TP
reproctl restart \(enall
Restart the Tilt daemon with the same services.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-start\f[R](1),
\f[B]reproctl\-stop\f[R](1)
